# The roadmap's criterion for stage 5, as TASK-14 makes it: a terminal window
# runs zosh, and keys typed into the window run commands, the file commands
# among them. The screen is read back by exact glyph match (see
# tools/test-runner/src/gui.rs). The serial line's input is closed: keys
# reach zosh only through the window (INV-0097-3). Rebuilt for the native
# shell in TASK-18 step 6.
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
# Above and left of the window: the background. The window's frame: the
# focused colour (ADR-0093, ADR-0094).
region 0 0 1024 14 203040
region 0 0 14 768 203040
region 15 15 970 1 40a0ff
region 15 15 1 490 40a0ff
type echo hi > a.txt\r
screen ~> _
# cat is a program: its output comes back to the window through zosh's
# relay of its out stream (ADR-0152 rule 1, TASK-18 step 8).
type cat a.txt\r
screen hi
screen ~> _
# F12 with one window: focus stays, and typing goes on. (That F12 never reaches a
# client is checked by t_gui: the terminal would send nothing for it anyway.)
key f12
type ls | search a\r
screen a.txt
screen ~> _
# exit closes the window, and init opens a new one with a new shell, since it
# was the last (ADR-0155's Decision, INV-0155-5).
type exit\r
serial init: shell ended
window
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type echo again\r
screen again
screen ~> _
latency 10
type poweroff\r
exit
